    "updated_at": "2026-11-20T13:24:25Z",
    "body": "Correction and more facts, from a read of `main` at `61a817bed`:\n\n- One line of the issue body is wrong. The test `lathe_post_tormach_thread.rs:282-285` sets `start_in_air = true` for the Fanuc script (line 288). It is not evidence for the Tormach post.\n- The defect itself stands. `assets/posts/tormach-lathe.cps:849` writes a `G0` to the start and lines 851-859 write the one-block `G76`. The script does not read `StartInAir`, so it has no refusal for the start.\n- The golden `thread_g76_mm.nc` has `G0 Z14` and `G76` on a bar of diameter 12 from Z-16 to Z40 (`tormach_lathe_support/mod.rs:132-175`). The start is in solid material. The inch twin has `G0 Z0.5512`.\n- Only two posts write a thread cycle: `fanuc-lathe.cps` (repaired by PR #2892) and `tormach-lathe.cps`. The `G33.1` in `linuxcnc.cps` is a rigid tap.\n- The value is ready for the post: `start_in_air` is in the CL record (`crates/cl/src/cl/thread.rs:154`) and reaches the script as `p.StartInAir` (`crates/post/src/post/cnc_thread.rs:111`).\n- No Tormach test pins the start of a `G76` cycle.\n",
